{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Cartographer's Algorithm","logline":"When cartographer Veya's wind-reading algorithm predicts the isles' drift and the collapse of the skybridges, she must prove it before toll-master Kael and the Drift Cartel bury her charts and seize the last stable routes.","theme":"Truth hoarded is power; truth shared is safety.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Prediction","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_forecast","title":"The Forecast","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya feeds years of her late mentor's observations and her own wind-sight readings into an algorithm that predicts how the isles will drift. The model forecasts that several skybridges will fail within the season.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Validate her mentor's theory that the isles are drifting apart by producing a working predictive model.","conflict":"The model's results contradict the Academy's accepted charts, and Veya's stubbornness makes her dismiss early signs that her data is incomplete.","outcome":"The algorithm predicts a collapse of the main trade bridges, giving Veya a forecast she must now prove with real-world evidence."},{"id":"scn_docks_ledger","title":"The Toll-Master's Ledger","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael notices irregular shipping patterns and hears rumours that a Silverspine cartographer is predicting bridge failures. He realises such a forecast could break the Cartel's hold on trade, or hand it the last stable routes if he controls it first.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Secure the Cartel's monopoly by learning what the cartographers know before the bridges collapse.","conflict":"His ledger-mastery shows him the Cartel's position is fragile, but he cannot reveal weakness to the other merchant princes.","outcome":"Kael resolves to obtain Veya's charts and sends word that her work should be watched.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_forecast"]},{"id":"scn_docks_confrontation","title":"Old Apprentices","summary":"Kael visits Silverspine and offers Veya funding and protection for her charts in exchange for exclusive control. Veya, who was his fellow apprentice, refuses. Both admire and distrust each other.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to obtain the charts; Veya wants to keep them out of Cartel hands.","conflict":"Kael's charm tempts her with recognition, which she wants, but she fears turning into the ambitious cartel leaders he represents.","outcome":"Veya refuses and the Cartel begins suppressing her work. Veya realises she needs independent proof and allies outside the Academy.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_forecast","scn_docks_ledger"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"The Race","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_alliance","title":"Secret Paths","summary":"Veya travels to The Hollow, where Maris, a miller's daughter, is smuggling grain to dodge the Cartel levy. Veya trades her wind-current knowledge for Maris's knowledge of unmapped service corridors, and they agree to cooperate.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants a way to reach distant isles unseen; Maris wants to keep The Hollow fed through the crisis.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly, and Veya's pride makes her reluctant to admit she needs help.","outcome":"They forge an alliance: Maris will guide Veya along hidden corridors while Veya helps predict safe grain routes.","depends_on":["scn_docks_confrontation"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_cables","title":"Frayed Cables","summary":"Using Maris's paths, Veya reaches Emberroost, where Bridge Wardens braid cloudstone cables. She tests her algorithm against the strain readings of worn cables and the Wardens' maintenance records, and finds close matches.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Obtain physical evidence that supports the algorithm's predictions.","conflict":"The Wardens are short on supplies, and the shielded forge-pits forbid open flame, so Veya must work within strict safety rules while Kael's interference has left the Wardens suspicious of outsiders.","outcome":"The data confirms the first predicted failure, but the Wardens warn that the Cartel has been withholding supplies and that Kael is blamed for it.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_alliance"]},{"id":"scn_docks_enforcers","title":"Cartel Enforcers","summary":"Kael learns of Veya's alliance and sends Cartel enforcers to close in on Maris's smuggling routes. Maris must choose between hiding her routes to protect The Hollow and sharing them with Veya.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to cut off Veya's access to routes; Maris wants to deliver grain and escape the enforcers.","conflict":"Maris's slow trust and unforgiving nature clash with her friendship for Veya, and Kael's pragmatism makes him exploit it.","outcome":"Maris escapes with partial cargo, but the Cartel now knows several of her corridors and shuts them down.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_cables"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_error","title":"The Wrong Prediction","summary":"Veya's next predicted failure does not occur on schedule. She refuses to admit the algorithm has a flaw, and the Academy council uses the miss to discredit her. Maris urges her to review the data.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to defend her model before the Academy; Maris wants her to correct it.","conflict":"Veya's inability to admit error leaves her isolated, and Maris's patience wears thin.","outcome":"Veya finally finds that her model omitted cloudstone fatigue data from Emberroost, and she corrects it, which gives a more accurate forecast but a sooner collapse date.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_cables","scn_docks_enforcers"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_choice","title":"Hiding in the Mills","summary":"Kael arrives at The Hollow with the grain levy and demands Veya's charts in exchange for lifting it. Veya, hiding in the windmills with Maris, must decide whether to hand over her work or trust that sharing it publicly is safer.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants the charts to seize the last stable routes; Veya wants to publish them without losing Maris's home.","conflict":"Kael's offer is tempting and he admits he admires her skill but cannot let her succeed; Maris's loyalty to home is tested.","outcome":"Veya refuses, Maris hides the charts in the mill corridors, and Kael vows to take the Academy's council vote on route control, setting up a public confrontation.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_error"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Reckoning","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_hearing","title":"The Public Hearing","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya presents her corrected algorithm to the council, Wardens, and merchants, while Kael argues that the Cartel must control the remaining routes. A predicted skybridge failure is scheduled for that hour.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to prove the drift is real and share the safe routes; Kael wants to block her and take control of the stable routes.","conflict":"Kael exposes her earlier error to discredit her, and Veya must admit it openly while Maris reveals the hidden corridors to back her up.","outcome":"The predicted bridge fails exactly on schedule, validating the algorithm and shattering Kael's argument that regulation can hold the network together.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_choice"]},{"id":"scn_bridge_crossing","title":"The Last Safe Route","summary":"With a collapsing bridge stranding travellers, Veya charts a safe route while Kael, seeing his control fail, must decide whether to withhold Cartel shipping lanes or open them for the evacuation.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to chart a safe route through the breaking network; Kael wants to seize the last stable routes.","conflict":"Kael's flaw of equating price with worth makes him demand payment, but he realises control now costs more than it gains.","outcome":"Kael opens the Cartel's lanes for the evacuation and Veya shares her charts openly, saving the stranded travellers.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_hearing"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The New Map","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_rebuilding","title":"Braiding Anew","summary":"At Emberroost, Wardens and Cartel merchants begin braiding new skybridges along Veya's predicted drift paths. Kael delivers supplies and settles the wind-debt owed to the Wardens in goods.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Rebuild the network along routes the algorithm shows will remain stable.","conflict":"Kael's reduced authority within the Cartel and Wardens' lingering distrust make cooperation uneasy.","outcome":"A fragile truce forms between the Wardens and the Cartel's reformers, and Veya's charts become public knowledge.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Open Granaries","summary":"Back in The Hollow, the grain levy is lifted. Maris no longer needs to smuggle and opens the granaries to share with other isles, accepting that hiding was brave but standing openly is bravery too.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants to ensure The Hollow is fed, and Veya wants to thank her and share credit.","conflict":"Maris has been slow to forgive Veya's earlier stubbornness, and Veya must prove she has changed.","outcome":"Maris forgives Veya, and The Hollow becomes a trusted node in the new network.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_rebuilding"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_legacy","title":"The Mentor's Legacy","summary":"Veya publishes her mentor's theory and her corrected algorithm in the Academy archive, crediting everyone who helped. Kael visits as a former rival and acknowledges the cost of control.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to honour her mentor by sharing the truth openly.","conflict":"Her old need for personal recognition tempts her to claim sole credit, while Kael's pride makes his acknowledgement difficult.","outcome":"Veya shares credit, Kael steps back from toll-mastery to help chart the new routes, and the isles continue drifting with a map everyone can read.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_harvest"]}]}]}
</Output>
