Mills","summary":"Kael arrives at The Hollow with the grain levy and demands Veya's charts in exchange for lifting it. Veya, hiding in the windmills with Maris, must decide whether to hand over her work or trust that sharing it publicly is safer.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants the charts to seize the last stable routes; Veya wants to publish them without losing Maris's home.","conflict":"Kael's offer is tempting and he admits he admires her skill but cannot let her succeed; Maris's loyalty to home is tested.","outcome":"Veya refuses, Maris hides the charts in the mill corridors, and Kael vows to take the Academy's council vote on route control, setting up a public confrontation.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_error"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Reckoning","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_hearing","title":"The Public Hearing","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya presents her corrected algorithm to the council, Wardens, and merchants, while Kael argues that the Cartel must control the remaining routes. A predicted skybridge failure is scheduled for that hour.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to prove the drift is real and share the safe routes; Kael wants to block her and take control of the stable routes.","conflict":"Kael exposes her earlier error to discredit her, and Veya must admit it openly while Maris reveals the hidden corridors to back her up.","outcome":"The predicted bridge fails exactly on schedule, validating the algorithm and shattering Kael's argument that regulation can hold the network together.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_choice"]},{"id":"scn_bridge_crossing","title":"The Last Safe Route","summary":"With a collapsing bridge stranding travellers, Veya charts a safe route while Kael, seeing his control fail, must decide whether to withhold Cartel shipping lanes or open them for the evacuation.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to chart a safe route through the breaking network; Kael wants to seize the last stable routes.","conflict":"Kael's flaw of equating price with worth makes him demand payment, but he realises control now costs more than it gains.","outcome":"Kael opens the Cartel's lanes for the evacuation and Veya shares her charts openly, saving the stranded travellers.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_hearing"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The New Map","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_rebuilding","title":"Braiding Anew","summary":"At Emberroost, Wardens and Cartel merchants begin braiding new skybridges along Veya's predicted drift paths. Kael delivers supplies and settles the wind-debt owed to the Wardens in goods.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Rebuild the network along routes the algorithm shows will remain stable.","conflict":"Kael's reduced authority within the Cartel and Wardens' lingering distrust make cooperation uneasy.","outcome":"A fragile truce forms between the Wardens and the Cartel's reformers, and Veya's charts become public knowledge.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Open Granaries","summary":"Back in The Hollow, the grain levy is lifted. Maris no longer needs to smuggle and opens the granaries to share with other isles, accepting that hiding was brave but standing openly is bravery too.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants to ensure The Hollow is fed, and Veya wants to thank her and share credit.","conflict":"Maris has been slow to forgive Veya's earlier stubbornness, and Veya must prove she has changed.","outcome":"Maris forgives Veya, and The Hollow becomes a trusted node in the new network.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_rebuilding"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_legacy","title":"The Mentor's Legacy","summary":"Veya publishes her mentor's theory and her corrected algorithm in the Academy archive, crediting everyone who helped. Kael visits as a former rival and acknowledges the cost of control.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to honour her mentor by sharing the truth openly.","conflict":"Her old need for personal recognition tempts her to claim sole credit, while Kael's pride makes his acknowledgement difficult.","outcome":"Veya shares credit, Kael steps back from toll-mastery to help chart the new routes, and the isles continue drifting with a map everyone can read.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_harvest"]}]}]}
