{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"Woven Destinies","logline":"As the skybridges begin to fail, a stubborn cartographer, a smuggling miller's daughter and a ruthless toll-master must each learn that their separate schemes are threads of a single spell, and that only by weaving them together can the archipelago be saved from drifting apart.","theme":"What is hoarded unravels; what is shared holds fast.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"Loose Threads","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_fading_charts","title":"The Fading Charts","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya uses her wind-sight to read the currents and finds a new pattern: the skybridges are breaking along a line that supports her late mentor's theory that the isles are drifting apart.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Chart a safe route through the breaking skybridge network by confirming the pattern in the wind currents.","conflict":"The pattern points to collapse, and Veya's stubbornness makes her reluctant to show unfinished work to anyone who might question it.","outcome":"Veya completes a first rough chart showing the last stable routes, and decides to keep it secret until it is flawless."},{"id":"scn_toll_master","title":"The Toll-Master's Ledger","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael raises skybridge tolls and uses his ledger-mastery to find the weak points in the merchants' contracts. He hears that Veya has been mapping the failing bridges.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Secure the Cartel's monopoly by locking down the last stable skybridge routes.","conflict":"He needs accurate charts to know which routes will survive, but the only cartographer able to make them is the rival he admires and cannot trust.","outcome":"Kael resolves to obtain Veya's charts, by offer or by pressure, and sends word to Silverspine."},{"id":"scn_grain_levy","title":"Grain Beneath the Floor","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris learns that Cartel enforcers will collect the grain levy at the next drift. She opens a hidden silo and plans to smuggle grain along unmapped service corridors.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Smuggle enough grain to keep The Hollow fed through the crisis.","conflict":"The enforcers are watching the known routes, and Maris trusts slowly, so she has no one to help her find a safe way out.","outcome":"Maris decides to carry the first load herself toward Silverspine, where she has heard a cartographer is mapping bridges the Cartel does not control.","depends_on":["scn_toll_master"]},{"id":"scn_cartel_offer","title":"An Offer at Silverspine","summary":"Kael arrives at Silverspine to propose a partnership in which his gold would fund Veya's charts in exchange for exclusive use. Veya refuses.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to buy Veya's charts, and Veya wants to keep them out of Cartel hands.","conflict":"They were once apprentices together. Kael's admiration and Veya's pride make the talk personal, and she cannot admit that she needs resources to finish the work.","outcome":"Veya refuses and Kael leaves with a veiled warning that the charts will not stay hers for long. She realises she must move her work out of the academy.","depends_on":["scn_fading_charts","scn_toll_master"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Tightening the Weave","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_meeting_on_the_bridge","title":"Crossing in the Dark","summary":"Veya travels toward Emberroost on a failing skybridge and meets Maris, who is fleeing enforcers with her grain. Each sees that the other has what she needs, and they trade wind-current knowledge for secret paths.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants a route that avoids Cartel watchers, and Maris wants a way past the enforcers.","conflict":"Maris is wary and slow to trust Veya, and Veya's stubbornness makes her reluctant to accept help.","outcome":"They agree to an uneasy alliance, taking on a shared wind-debt that each must repay in labour or goods within a season.","depends_on":["scn_grain_levy","scn_cartel_offer"]},{"id":"scn_forge_sabotage","title":"Cables at Emberroost","summary":"At Emberroost, the Bridge Wardens accuse Kael of sabotaging supplies of cloudstone. Veya and Maris arrive to find the braiding forges short of materials and the Wardens on the edge of open war with the Cartel.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants the Wardens to act on her charts. Kael wants to deflect the sabotage claims and Maris wants to resupply her isle.","conflict":"Kael denies the charge with charm, Veya cannot bring herself to concede that her chart is incomplete, and the Wardens will not trust the word of a cartographer who hoards her work.","outcome":"The Wardens grant a brief truce but demand proof. Kael slips away, and he has seen Maris's grain routes and part of Veya's chart.","depends_on":["scn_meeting_on_the_bridge"]},{"id":"scn_enforcers_close_in","title":"The Routes Burn","summary":"Using what he saw at Emberroost, Kael has enforcers close the grain routes and seize Maris's silos in The Hollow. Maris learns that her trust in Veya has put her home at risk.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants to protect the silos, and Veya wants to help her without revealing the full chart.","conflict":"Maris, who rarely forgives, blames Veya for the leak, and Veya is unable to admit that her secrecy and pride were part of the cause.","outcome":"Maris breaks with Veya and sets out alone, choosing home over friendship. Veya is left with a half-finished chart and a debt she cannot repay.","depends_on":["scn_forge_sabotage"]},{"id":"scn_veyas_error","title":"The Chart That Failed","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Veya tests her chart against the bridges and it fails: a span collapses because she misjudged a current. Kael sees the failure and offers to help her, at a price.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to prove her chart is sound, and Kael wants to take control of it while she is vulnerable.","conflict":"She cannot admit she is wrong, and he equates price with worth. Each of them hesitates because they still respect the other.","outcome":"Veya refuses the price, but finally admits the error to herself. She decides the chart can only work if it is combined with Maris's paths and the Wardens' knowledge.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_close_in"]},{"id":"scn_maris_alone","title":"The Hidden Corridors","summary":"Maris takes the unmapped service corridors to carry the last grain reserves out of the enforcers' reach. She finds that the corridors run alongside the failing bridges and that they hold the bridges' weak joints.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Hide enough grain to keep The Hollow fed.","conflict":"Hiding alone is not enough, since the grain cannot be moved without crossing bridges that may collapse, and her slow trust leaves her isolated.","outcome":"Maris realises the corridors and Veya's chart describe the same network. She decides to seek out Veya, despite her anger.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_close_in"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Spell Completed","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_three_threads","title":"Three Threads Meet","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya, Maris and Kael face each other as the main span of the skybridge network begins to fail. Veya offers her chart, Maris offers her corridors, and Kael holds the ledger that records every route and debt. The Wardens will act only if all three are shared.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to chart a safe route, Maris wants to feed her isle, and Kael wants to hold the last stable routes.","conflict":"Each holds one thread and will not give it up first. Kael's belief that everything has a price is set against Veya's pride and Maris's refusal to forgive.","outcome":"Veya admits her mistake and shares her chart openly. Maris, moved by this, shares her paths, and Kael, seeing that control will not save the bridges, hands over his ledger.","depends_on":["scn_veyas_error","scn_maris_alone"]},{"id":"scn_weaving","title":"The Second Weaving","summary":"Using the chart to find the weak joints, the corridors to reach them and the ledger to marshal the labour and cloudstone, the three work with the Wardens at the forge-pits to braid new cables and rejoin the failing span before it breaks.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Rebuild the failing span before the isles drift beyond reach, using all three threads together.","conflict":"The work must be done without open flame outside the shielded forge-pits, and time is short. A single mistake from any of them could sever the bridge.","outcome":"The span holds. The three threads together complete the spell, and the main routes are saved for everyone.","depends_on":["scn_three_threads"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What Holds","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_wind_debt_repaid","title":"Debts Repaid","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael answers to the Cartel for giving up his ledger. He uses it to lower the tolls and to set the grain levy aside in return for labour on the bridges, and he accepts the cost of losing his monopoly.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to settle the debts the crisis created without losing everything, and Veya wants the routes kept open to all.","conflict":"The Cartel princes resist giving up control, and Kael must accept that he has lost his monopoly.","outcome":"Tolls are cut and the levy is lifted. Kael learns that control costs more than it gains, and Veya's charts are published for all.","depends_on":["scn_weaving"]},{"id":"scn_homecoming","title":"Grain for Half the Sky","summary":"Maris returns to The Hollow and the windmills grind freely again. She opens her hidden silos and shows others the corridors, learning that hiding can be as brave as standing still, and that sharing can be braver.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants to feed her isle openly, and Veya wants to repay her wind-debt and mend the friendship.","conflict":"Maris still struggles to forgive, and Veya must find a way to repay what she owes without taking credit.","outcome":"Veya repays her debt in labour at the windmills, and Maris forgives her. The friendship is restored on honest terms.","depends_on":["scn_wind_debt_repaid"]},{"id":"scn_new_charts","title":"A Map for Everyone","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya hangs her finished charts in the open, crediting Maris and Kael, and teaches students to read the currents. Her late mentor's theory is proven, and the isles keep drifting but stay joined.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to share her work and honour her mentor's theory, with her friends beside her.","conflict":"Veya's old craving for recognition tempts her to take sole credit, and she must choose to share it instead.","outcome":"Veya learns that some truths are safer shared than hoarded. The three threads of the spell are woven into one lasting network for the archipelago.","depends_on":["scn_homecoming"]}]}]}
