llapses because she misjudged a current. Kael sees the failure and offers to help her, at a price.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to prove her chart is sound, and Kael wants to take control of it while she is vulnerable.","conflict":"She cannot admit she is wrong, and he equates price with worth. Each of them hesitates because they still respect the other.","outcome":"Veya refuses the price, but finally admits the error to herself. She decides the chart can only work if it is combined with Maris's paths and the Wardens' knowledge.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_close_in"]},{"id":"scn_maris_alone","title":"The Hidden Corridors","summary":"Maris takes the unmapped service corridors to carry the last grain reserves out of the enforcers' reach. She finds that the corridors run alongside the failing bridges and that they hold the bridges' weak joints.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Hide enough grain to keep The Hollow fed.","conflict":"Hiding alone is not enough, since the grain cannot be moved without crossing bridges that may collapse, and her slow trust leaves her isolated.","outcome":"Maris realises the corridors and Veya's chart describe the same network. She decides to seek out Veya, despite her anger.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_close_in"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Spell Completed","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_three_threads","title":"Three Threads Meet","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya, Maris and Kael face each other as the main span of the skybridge network begins to fail. Veya offers her chart, Maris offers her corridors, and Kael holds the ledger that records every route and debt. The Wardens will act only if all three are shared.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to chart a safe route, Maris wants to feed her isle, and Kael wants to hold the last stable routes.","conflict":"Each holds one thread and will not give it up first. Kael's belief that everything has a price is set against Veya's pride and Maris's refusal to forgive.","outcome":"Veya admits her mistake and shares her chart openly. Maris, moved by this, shares her paths, and Kael, seeing that control will not save the bridges, hands over his ledger.","depends_on":["scn_veyas_error","scn_maris_alone"]},{"id":"scn_weaving","title":"The Second Weaving","summary":"Using the chart to find the weak joints, the corridors to reach them and the ledger to marshal the labour and cloudstone, the three work with the Wardens at the forge-pits to braid new cables and rejoin the failing span before it breaks.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Rebuild the failing span before the isles drift beyond reach, using all three threads together.","conflict":"The work must be done without open flame outside the shielded forge-pits, and time is short. A single mistake from any of them could sever the bridge.","outcome":"The span holds. The three threads together complete the spell, and the main routes are saved for everyone.","depends_on":["scn_three_threads"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What Holds","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_wind_debt_repaid","title":"Debts Repaid","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael answers to the Cartel for giving up his ledger. He uses it to lower the tolls and to set the grain levy aside in return for labour on the bridges, and he accepts the cost of losing his monopoly.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to settle the debts the crisis created without losing everything, and Veya wants the routes kept open to all.","conflict":"The Cartel princes resist giving up control, and Kael must accept that he has lost his monopoly.","outcome":"Tolls are cut and the levy is lifted. Kael learns that control costs more than it gains, and Veya's charts are published for all.","depends_on":["scn_weaving"]},{"id":"scn_homecoming","title":"Grain for Half the Sky","summary":"Maris returns to The Hollow and the windmills grind freely again. She opens her hidden silos and shows others the corridors, learning that hiding can be as brave as standing still, and that sharing can be braver.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants to feed her isle openly, and Veya wants to repay her wind-debt and mend the friendship.","conflict":"Maris still struggles to forgive, and Veya must find a way to repay what she owes without taking credit.","outcome":"Veya repays her debt in labour at the windmills, and Maris forgives her. The friendship is restored on honest terms.","depends_on":["scn_wind_debt_repaid"]},{"id":"scn_new_charts","title":"A Map for Everyone","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya hangs her finished charts in the open, crediting Maris and Kael, and teaches students to read the currents. Her late mentor's theory is proven, and the isles keep drifting but stay joined.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to share her work and honour her mentor's theory, with her friends beside her.","conflict":"Veya's old craving for recognition tempts her to take sole credit, and she must choose to share it instead.","outcome":"Veya learns that some truths are safer shared than hoarded. The three threads of the spell are woven into one lasting network for the archipelago.","depends_on":["scn_homecoming"]}]}]}
