lished for all.","depends_on":["scn_weaving"]},{"id":"scn_homecoming","title":"Grain for Half the Sky","summary":"Maris returns to The Hollow and the windmills grind freely again. She opens her hidden silos and shows others the corridors, learning that hiding can be as brave as standing still, and that sharing can be braver.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants to feed her isle openly, and Veya wants to repay her wind-debt and mend the friendship.","conflict":"Maris still struggles to forgive, and Veya must find a way to repay what she owes without taking credit.","outcome":"Veya repays her debt in labour at the windmills, and Maris forgives her. The friendship is restored on honest terms.","depends_on":["scn_wind_debt_repaid"]},{"id":"scn_new_charts","title":"A Map for Everyone","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya hangs her finished charts in the open, crediting Maris and Kael, and teaches students to read the currents. Her late mentor's theory is proven, and the isles keep drifting but stay joined.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to share her work and honour her mentor's theory, with her friends beside her.","conflict":"Veya's old craving for recognition tempts her to take sole credit, and she must choose to share it instead.","outcome":"Veya learns that some truths are safer shared than hoarded. The three threads of the spell are woven into one lasting network for the archipelago.","depends_on":["scn_homecoming"]}]}]}
