_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to assess the damage and prove the bridges are failing naturally; Maris wants to avoid being blamed for the Hollow's smuggling.","conflict":"The Wardens suspect Cartel sabotage and Veya's reading is not yet certain. She will not admit uncertainty, and the dispute raises tension among the factions.","outcome":"Veya's reading shows the cable failed through strain, not sabotage. The Wardens, still angry at the Cartel, call for a council at Emberroost.","depends_on":["scn_veya_meets_maris"]},{"id":"scn_kael_confronts_veya","title":"Kael Names His Price","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael confronts Veya with a Cartel offer. He will protect her charts and grant her safe passage if she hands them over, or the Cartel will seize them. Maris's smuggling is used as leverage.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants the charts to secure Cartel control of the stable routes; Veya wants to leave with her work and her friend intact.","conflict":"Kael's charm hides a threat, and he equates price with worth. Veya's refusal to admit her error in dealing with him leaves them exposed to his ledger-mastery.","outcome":"Veya and Maris escape with the charts after Maris leads them through a dock service corridor. Kael realises the three factions could unite against him, and Veya sees that the Cartel will not stop.","depends_on":["scn_forge_pit_sabotage"]},{"id":"scn_wardens_demand_council","title":"The Wardens' Ultimatum","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya argues with her own Wardens, who want to bury the Cartel and withhold the charts as a weapon. She is tempted to hoard the charts as Kael would, and Maris urges her to share them.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the Wardens' backing without surrendering control of her charts; Maris wants a truce that ends the grain levy.","conflict":"Veya fears becoming like the ambitious cartel leaders, yet cannot admit her hoarding is the same instinct. Maris's loyalty to The Hollow strains against her friendship with Veya.","outcome":"Veya agrees to carry the charts to a three-faction council at Emberroost. The Wardens reluctantly agree to a truce meeting.","depends_on":["scn_kael_confronts_veya"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Emberroost Accord","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_council_at_emberroost","title":"The Council Convenes","summary":"The Bridge Wardens, Drift Cartel, and Hollow Circle gather at Emberroost. Kael argues for Cartel control of the routes, and Veya's charts show that no faction can hold the network alone.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the three factions to agree to a shared truce; Kael wants the Cartel to hold the last stable routes.","conflict":"Kael uses ledger-mastery to find the weak points in every arrangement, and Veya's pride tempts her to dismiss his counter-arguments instead of admitting her chart has errors.","outcome":"Kael exposes an error in Veya's chart, which she grudgingly admits. The council nearly collapses and a bridge cable groans under the strain.","depends_on":["scn_wardens_demand_council"]},{"id":"scn_the_accord_forged","title":"The Accord Is Forged","summary":"With a cable failing, Veya shares her corrected charts openly, Maris guides the factions along her service corridors, and Kael sees that control costs more than it gains. The three factions sign the Emberroost Accord, which shares the stable routes, caps tolls, and eases the grain levy.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Secure a truce that keeps the skybridges standing before they fail.","conflict":"Kael must give up the monopoly he has fought for, and Veya must share the work she wanted recognition for. Wind-debt and the ban on open flame mean the repair must be done carefully in the forge-pit.","outcome":"The factions sign the Accord and the Wardens, Cartel, and Hollow Circle begin repairs, with wind-debts repaid in labour.","depends_on":["scn_council_at_emberroost"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"Bridges Mended","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_pays_the_price","title":"Kael's Reckoning","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael faces the Cartel's toll-masters, who object to the Accord. He chooses to honour it, and in doing so loses part of his old power while gaining a more durable position.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Persuade the Cartel to honour the Accord despite lost monopoly profits.","conflict":"Kael's belief that price equals worth makes him doubt the value of shared stability, and his rivals call him weak.","outcome":"The Cartel grudgingly accepts the Accord and Kael accepts a lesser role, understanding that control costs more than it gains.","depends_on":["scn_the_accord_forged"]},{"id":"scn_the_hollow_fed","title":"Grain Without Smuggling","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris sees the first legal grain shipments pass under the eased levy. Her secret corridors are no longer needed for smuggling, and she accepts that hiding can be as brave as standing still.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Confirm that The Hollow will be fed under the Accord.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and rarely forgives, so she must decide whether to trust the Cartel's promises and keep her friendship with Veya.","outcome":"Maris trusts the new arrangement and keeps her corridors in reserve. Her friendship with Veya is secure.","depends_on":["scn_the_accord_forged","scn_kael_pays_the_price"]},{"id":"scn_charts_shared","title":"Charts for Every Isle","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya copies her corrected charts for every faction. She accepts her mentor's theory in a form she can share, and she understands that some truths are safer shared than hoarded.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Distribute the charts so every isle can navigate the breaking network.","conflict":"Veya wants the credit for her mentor's theory, yet sharing the charts means giving up control of them. Kael arrives to offer the Cartel's help with distribution.","outcome":"Veya shares the charts openly, and Kael's rival-turned-partner helps carry them across the archipelago. The skybridges hold for another season.","depends_on":["scn_the_hollow_fed"]}]}]}
