 cartel figure and refuses, but her need for passage leaves her with a wind-debt.","outcome":"Veya leaves with passage and a wind-debt to the Cartel. Kael learns the chart exists and sets enforcers to watch her.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_chart"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_silo","title":"Grain in the Dark","summary":"Veya's route detours through The Hollow, where Maris is moving smuggled grain past Cartel levy collectors. Veya trades wind-current knowledge for Maris's unmapped service corridors. Maris, slow to trust, tests her before agreeing.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Maris wants to smuggle enough grain to keep The Hollow fed. Veya wants a hidden path that avoids Cartel watchers.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya is a Cartel spy because of the wind-debt, and Veya's pride makes her bristle at being doubted.","outcome":"They form an uneasy alliance: Maris will guide Veya through the corridors, and Veya will read the winds for Maris's grain runs.","depends_on":["scn_docks_toll"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"The Weight of Crossing","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_cables","title":"Cables That Sing","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya and Maris show the Bridge Wardens the chart. The wardens, who are accusing Kael of sabotaging forge-island supplies, find the cloudstone cables short of supply and strained. Veya's data shows the bridge cannot be reinforced in time, yet cannot be abandoned either.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the wardens to validate her chart and reinforce the central skybridge.","conflict":"The wardens lack cables because of Cartel interference, and Veya's refusal to admit that her first reading was incomplete makes them doubt the whole chart.","outcome":"The wardens agree only to a partial reinforcement. Veya learns the span's failure is tied to the load of the crossings, and she must find a way to reduce traffic.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_silo"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_ambush","title":"Enforcers in the Windmills","summary":"Kael's enforcers, following Veya's wind-debt, close in on Maris's smuggling routes in The Hollow. Kael arrives to press Veya, torn between admiration for her skill and the need to stop her.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants Veya's chart and Maris's routes to seize the last stable crossings. Maris wants to protect her isle.","conflict":"Kael's internal conflict makes him hesitate to harm Veya, while Maris must choose between hiding her routes to save home and standing with Veya.","outcome":"Maris leads Veya out through a service corridor, but at the cost of exposing one silo. Kael takes the exposed grain and the knowledge that Veya's chart is real.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_cables"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_archive","title":"The Mentor's Margin","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine and finds in her late mentor's notes that the isles drift apart even as the bridges hold, because the bridges are rewoven by every crossing's wind-debt. She sees that her own certainty was the error, but resists saying so aloud.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants proof that her mentor's theory resolves the contradiction in her chart.","conflict":"The notes imply her first reading was wrong, and her flaw makes her hide it even from Maris, who senses the lie and begins to withdraw her trust.","outcome":"Veya understands the paradox: the span will collapse as an object and stand as a shared work. Her concealment damages her friendship with Maris.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_ambush"]},{"id":"scn_docks_ultimatum","title":"The Price of the Last Bridge","summary":"Kael confronts Veya at Mistral Docks. He demands the chart in exchange for cancelling her wind-debt and sparing The Hollow's grain. Veya, hoarding her discovery, nearly accepts.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to buy the chart and close the deal before the bridges fall. Veya wants to protect Maris's isle without giving up her recognition.","conflict":"Veya's pride and fear of obscurity pull her toward the bargain, while Maris, who feels betrayed by her concealment, threatens to leave.","outcome":"Veya stalls and flees with Maris's reluctant help. Kael, certain the central skybridge is the last stable route, moves to take it and its toll.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_archive"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Span at Dawn","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_forge","title":"A Spark Above the Pit","summary":"Kael's crew attempts to seal the central skybridge for the Cartel's exclusive use and a spark from an unshielded lantern threatens to sever it. Veya, Maris and the wardens race to shield the forge-pit and the anchors, in line with the rule against open flame aloft.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to keep the bridge from breaking. Kael wants to take control of it before it collapses.","conflict":"Sealing the span doubles its load and guarantees collapse, while releasing it means giving up Kael's monopoly and Veya's sole claim to the chart.","outcome":"The bridge begins to fail. Veya finally admits she was wrong about the chart and offers it openly, and Kael sees that his control will cost him the span.","depends_on":["scn_docks_ultimatum"]},{"id":"scn_central_span","title":"The Bridge That Is and Is Not","summary":"On the central skybridge, Veya publishes the chart to everyone crossing and asks each to leave the span by their own route, each repaying their wind-debt by carrying a strand of the cable to a new anchor. Kael chooses to give up the toll and carry a strand himself. Maris guides the crowd through her hidden corridors.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to get everyone off the span and keep its meaning alive. Kael must decide whether to hold the bridge or release it.","conflict":"Staying to hold the span would save the structure and doom its users, while leaving it spares them and lets it fall. Kael's flaw pulls him to price the choice, and Maris must trust Veya again.","outcome":"The old span collapses as the crowd crosses, and the strands they carry weave into a new span that stands. The bridge is both lost and kept because they chose it together.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_forge"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What Holds","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_new_charts","title":"A Chart Shared","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya redraws the network with the woven span at its center and opens the chart to the wardens, the Cartel and The Hollow alike. Maris contributes her service corridors, and Veya tells her openly that she was wrong.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to share the truth she once hoarded and repair her friendship with Maris.","conflict":"Sharing the chart means giving up sole recognition, and Maris, who rarely forgives, must decide whether Veya's admission is enough.","outcome":"Maris forgives Veya and the chart becomes common knowledge. Veya takes her mentor's theory as shared work and not as personal vindication.","depends_on":["scn_central_span"]},{"id":"scn_docks_ledger_closed","title":"The Ledger Closed","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael lowers the tolls on the woven span and cancels the wind-debts owed to the Cartel by those who carried the cable. He admits control cost more than it gained, and Veya's wind-debt is repaid by her strand.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to settle the Cartel's place in the new network without losing his standing. Veya wants her debt cleared.","conflict":"The Cartel's princes resist the lowered tolls, and Kael must accept a smaller, shared role in place of monopoly.","outcome":"The toll war eases. Kael accepts a modest regulated trade, and the old rivals part with respect.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_new_charts"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Windmills Turning","summary":"Back in The Hollow, Maris watches grain move openly across the new span with the levy lowered. She sees that her hiding was a kind of bravery and that standing in the open is another.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants The Hollow fed without having to smuggle.","conflict":"Her habit of hiding and slow trust make it hard to step into the open, even when the danger has passed.","outcome":"Maris lets Veya read the winds for the first open harvest run, and the isles keep drifting while the bridge holds.","depends_on":["scn_docks_ledger_closed"]}]}]}
